WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.720
Hello, my name is Youssef,

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.560
and I’m head of information systems at the Cheikh Zaid Foundation.

3
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.230
Regarding this candidate’s situation,

4
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:13.330
I think his reaction was not appropriate for a job interview.

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.720
You have to understand that when a candidate gets angry in front of a jury,

6
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.930
he gives a bad image of himself, even if he is right.

7
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:31.290
The jury may think he can’t handle stress or work under pressure.

8
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:38.570
Sometimes, a reaction like that can cost him his chance of being hired.

9
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.860
My advice to this candidate is simple:

10
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.000
when facing criticism, first, breathe,

11
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.540
stay seated and keep calm.

12
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.000
Then he can politely ask:

13
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:58.110
“Could you tell me which part of my answer wasn’t clear?”

14
00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:05.290
He can then go back over his explanation with simple examples and concrete facts.

15
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.790
And if he was wrong, it’s not a big deal.

16
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:15.150
What matters is admitting his mistake and apologising if necessary.

17
00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:20.630
In our work, we often face difficult situations.

18
00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:28.050
So you have to learn to listen, to stay calm and to communicate well with others.
